CHILD_OP_FOU_GUE_MCAST_RX             REASON: transient userns+netns grandchild install of a genl "fou" receive port + IPPROTO_RAW hand-rolled UDP-encap frames at a mcast outer dst; not safe for steady rotation until canary-queue load-tests the FOU/GUE hash + multicast walker interaction
CHILD_OP_GENEVE_RX                    REASON: transient userns+netns grandchild install of a geneve link (RTM_NEWLINK kind=geneve) + IPPROTO_RAW hand-rolled outer IPv4/UDP(6081)/GENEVE frames with variable-length options against 127.0.0.1; not safe for steady rotation until canary-queue load-tests the geneve option walker + inner-frame decap path
CHILD_OP_NETNS_MOUNTNS_SETUP_PROBE   REASON: net+mount ns setup-path race; per-child netns/mntns unshare not safe for steady rotation
CHILD_OP_BAREUDP_RX                   REASON: transient userns+netns grandchild install of a bareudp link (RTM_NEWLINK kind=bareudp) with picked port+ethertype+multiproto + IPPROTO_RAW hand-rolled outer IPv4/UDP/inner-L3 frames against 127.0.0.1; not safe for steady rotation until canary-queue load-tests the ethertype-branching decap + iptunnel_pull_header path
CHILD_OP_MPLS_LABEL_STACK_RX          REASON: transient userns+netns grandchild sysctl-writes net.mpls.platform_labels + net.mpls.conf.lo.input to enable MPLS RX on lo + AF_PACKET SOCK_RAW hand-rolled Ethernet(0x8847)/label-stack/inner-IPv4 frames; not safe for steady rotation until canary-queue load-tests the mpls_forward label-stack walker + inner-header peek
CHILD_OP_DEEP_PATH_NESTING            REASON: persistent deep-directory tree creation in scratch tmpdir + reader hammer at extreme cwd; per-invocation mkdir/chdir chain + partial-teardown residue not safe for steady rotation
CHILD_OP_ESPINTCP_COALESCE_CHURN      REASON: transient userns+netns grandchild install of TCP_ULP espintcp on both ends of a loopback TCP pair + TCP_CORK/TCP_NODELAY-toggled crafted length-prefixed frame bursts; net+ULP setup with coalesce-side pressure not safe for steady rotation until canary-queue load-tests the espintcp receive coalesce / page-cache reassembly path
CHILD_OP_CRED_TRANSITION_CHURN        REASON: mutates the calling task's credentials (capset re-installs a churned effective-cap subset + JOIN_SESSION_KEYRING rotates the caller's session keyring), then immediately drives a permission-sensitive op in the SAME task; not safe for steady rotation
CHILD_OP_NETDEV_NETNS_MIGRATE         REASON: migrates a virtual netdev (veth/vxlan/gretap) between two sibling user-namespace-owned network namespaces via RTM_SETLINK IFLA_NET_NS_FD, then drives the device from the target ns; per-invocation namespace churn + cross-ns device lifetime pressure not safe for steady rotation until canary-queue load-tests the cross-ns device refcount / dev_net(dev) migration paths
CHILD_OP_MAP_SHARED_STRESS            REASON: file-backed MAP_SHARED writeback race with sibling worker forks + MADV_DONTFORK fork COW-vs-shared split + O_APPEND-vs-mmap coherence burst; per-invocation fork storm + shared-inode pagecache pressure not safe for steady rotation until canary-queue load-tests the shared-writeback / VM_DONTCOPY / append-past-i_size ordering paths
CHILD_OP_TC_LIVE_TRAFFIC              REASON: transient userns+netns grandchild install of a private veth pair + clsact matchall-mirred action chain + mid-burst RTM_DELTFILTER / RTM_NEWTFILTER race against a live UDP burst, plus an opportunistic XDP-pass attach; per-invocation namespace churn + tcf_classify() action-chain race not safe for steady rotation until canary-queue load-tests the classifier update / lock-ordering paths
CHILD_OP_HFS_MOUNT_FUZZ               REASON: crafted-image mount fuzzer for a legacy on-disk filesystem; transient userns+mnt-ns grandchild swaps a memfd-backed image onto a scratch_block loop and drives mount("hfs") + option-parse + mdb-commit churn; image-mount lifecycle over a shared scratch loop is not safe for steady rotation until canary-queue load-tests the parse / mdb_commit paths
CHILD_OP_RDS_ZCOPY_CRAFTED_SEND       REASON: AF_RDS SO_ZEROCOPY sendmsg with a partially-mapped iovec deliberately faulting mid pin-walk; exercises rds_message_zcopy_from_user page-pin + rds_message_purge free path where refcount skew produces page double-free / put-of-freed-page under KASAN and must not run in steady rotation until the canary queue load-tests the per-page GUP unwind edge
CHILD_OP_NEXTHOP_REPLACE_CHURN        REASON: transient userns+netns grandchild forks an intra-ns route-churn worker while the parent hammers RTM_NEWNEXTHOP + NLM_F_REPLACE on a nh id whose f6i_list is non-empty; targets the nexthop-replace-notifier vs unlocked IPv6 route walk (fib6_check_nh_list vs fib6_purge_rt) UAF class, not safe for steady rotation until canary-queue load-tests the replace-notifier ordering
CHILD_OP_SEG6_END_DT4_RX              REASON: transient userns+netns grandchild install of a VRF + seg6local RTM_NEWROUTE (LWTUNNEL_ENCAP_SEG6_LOCAL / SEG6_LOCAL_ACTION_END_DT4 / vrftable=100) + AF_PACKET SOCK_RAW hand-rolled Ethernet/IPv6(nh=43)/SRH/inner-IPv4-with-IP-options frames at lo; targets the End.DT4 decap stale-IPCB overlay path (input_action_end_dt4 skips ip_rcv_core so __ip_options_echo reads options offset from IP6CB, KASAN slab-OOB), not safe for steady rotation until canary-queue load-tests the seg6local decap + inner-options path
CHILD_OP_CT_EXPECT_REALLOC            REASON: transient userns+netns grandchild + CTNETLINK CT_NEW+CTA_HELP / EXP_NEW / CT_NEW NLM_F_REPLACE+CTA_LABELS / EXP_DELETE sequence targeting the nf_conn_help expectation hlist backpointer vs nf_ct_ext_add krealloc race; per-invocation namespace churn + helper-ext realloc pressure not safe for steady rotation until canary-queue load-tests the hlist_add_head_rcu-vs-krealloc unlink ordering
CHILD_OP_INET_LISTENER_REHASH_RACE    REASON: pits concurrent AF_INET/AF_INET6 listener churn (bind+listen+close) against a SYN-flood driver and a bind+connect rehash driver on the same fixed port pool inside a single childop; targets the __inet_lookup_listener lhash2 walk vs unhash->ehash sk_nulls_node relink race that can return a TIME_WAIT sock to the listener lookup; four concurrent forked workers per invocation are not safe for steady rotation until canary-queue load-tests the burst
CHILD_OP_IP6_TUNNEL_CHURN             REASON: transient userns+netns grandchild install of an ip6ip6 tunnel (RTM_NEWLINK kind=ip6tnl, IFLA_IPTUN_PROTO=IPPROTO_IPV6) + raw ICMPv6 quote-carrying error burst (ip6ip6_err() stale skb->cb[] re-inject shape at net/ipv6/ip6_tunnel.c:612) and AF_PACKET ETH_P_ALL tap-forced skb head clone + UDPv6 sendmsg driving ip6_tnl_xmit() (missing skb_cow_head() shape); per-invocation namespace churn + tunnel lifecycle + raw-socket burst not safe for steady rotation until canary-queue load-tests the tunnel err re-inject and shared-head xmit paths
